  "description": "Offroad, on road, and everything in between, this tough hardtail is your little ripper’s ticket to ride. Whether they’re exploring trails or riding to school, the Speed 24 is solid little mountain bike that lets young riders enjoy the freedom of 2-wheels. Built with quality components and a light and strong aluminum frame, the Speed series is doesn’t skimp on quality because they are for kids. With disc brakes and front suspension, the Speed 24 is a great ride to gain confidence on and off the pavement.\n\nMEC designed frame uses 6061 aluminum for a durable yet light construction\n\nSR Suntour XCT suspension fork has 80mm of travel and preload adjustment for improved tracking\n\n9-speed Shimano Cues drivetrain provides smooth, reliable shifting, giving a great range for trails or hills\n\nThe Cues line provides reliable performance, durability, and easy maintenance – with cross compatibility across the line\n\nTektro hydraulic disc brakes have lots of stopping power in all weather\n\nWTB Ranger tires bite into dirt and gravel, and roll smoothly on paved surfaces\n\nSized for kids from 8 to 11 years, or about 135 to 150cm (4ft. 5in. to 4ft. 11in.)\n\nWheel size: 24in\n\nReflective details help keep your little rider seen\n\nBikes are covered by MEC's Rocksolid Guarantee and Bike Service Agreement. You can bring your bike to any MEC bike shop for free adjustments and minor maintenance for a year after purchase\n\nMEC bikes were designed in Canada. Everything from the frames to the graphics was developed at the MEC Head Office in Vancouver, BC\n\nDue to challenges with supply chain, components may be substituted for comparable parts at any time. The listed build is how MEC intended your bike to arrive, though the manufacturer may need to make a tweak or two to get you riding sooner",
